 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No present-day political reading; the treaty exception of 72 is kept («عهد مؤكد لم ينقضوه»). A house for «آووا», geometric for «والله بما تعملون بصير». No people drawn. STAGING v4: c1 (72): a town by day. Three believers walk in from the left on 72:4 (the emigrants; Al-Muyassar: to the land of Islam or a land where they can worship), under a footsteps plate that ends before the Name. Their striving with wealth and lives (72:5-7) is not pictured: no war. On 72:11 three believers of the town go to meet them (the helpers) under a house plate (72:12; Al-Muyassar: they lodged the emigrants in their homes) and hand them a purse on 72:13 (Al-Muyassar: they shared their wealth with them). A seal plate for the bond of alliance and love (72:15; As-Sa'di: a pact of alliance and love). 72:18-41 (believers who did not emigrate, help in religion, the treaty exception) gets camera only: those believers are not drawn and no fighting is shown; an hourglass for until they emigrate (72:28), a seal plate for the treaty (72:38, ending before the Name) and a geometric plate on the Name for All-Seeing (72:42). After the helpers move to the centre the right side is empty, so the camera only goes wide, close or to the left. c2 (73): three disbelievers gathered at the centre of a town (allies of one another; As-Sa'di: disbelief brought them together); the warning to the believers (73:6-13) is a condition, so nothing is acted; a wind plate for the trial and corruption (73:9) and the camera stays on the disbelievers, not on the believers. No present-day political reading."
 },
